  <section class="wrap fiche-body">
    <div>
      <h2>The vibe</h2>
      <p>Opened on 1 July 2026 and officially inaugurated on 30 July by the town hall, Pipady beach is Toulon's second dog beach, set on a cove at the foot of the Tour Royale. The 2000 m² space is fully fenced, which lets dogs roam off-leash safely, separated from other users of the site.</p>

      <h2>What to know before you go</h2>
      <p>Access is free and open year-round, every day. Clear signage organises the flow: swimmers and visitors are directed to the left, while a dedicated access on the right is reserved for dogs and their owners, to avoid conflicts between the two uses.</p>
      <div class="callout">Coco's tip: the site is very new (opened mid-2026), so still little known — the perfect spot to enjoy a real moment of freedom with your dog without too many people around.</div>

      <h2>Nearby</h2>
      <p>The Tour Royale, a 15th-century historic monument, overlooks the beach. Toulon's other dog beach, Anse Tabarly, is also in the Mourillon area, just a few minutes away.</p>
